From: Josh Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v8: stub WasmModuleCompilation when WebAssembly is disabled

Chromium 152's Blink script streamer (BackgroundWasmStreamManager) uses
v8::WasmModuleCompilation unconditionally, but V8 defines it only in
src/wasm/wasm-js.cc, which is not built with v8_enable_webassembly=false.
api.cc already stubs WasmStreaming for that configuration; add the same for
WasmModuleCompilation. Without it, linking v8_context_snapshot_generator
fails with undefined v8::WasmModuleCompilation symbols.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 v8/src/api/api.cc | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/api/api.cc b/v8/src/api/api.cc
--- a/v8/src/api/api.cc
+++ b/v8/src/api/api.cc
@@ -12329,6 +12329,35 @@
                                                      Local<Value> value) {
   FATAL("WebAssembly is disabled");
 }
+
+// Likewise WasmModuleCompilation, which Blink's script streamer holds for wasm
+// responses. With WebAssembly disabled no module can compile: accept and drop
+// the bytes, and resolve {Finish} with an error.
+class WasmModuleCompilation::Impl {};
+
+WasmModuleCompilation::WasmModuleCompilation() = default;
+
+WasmModuleCompilation::~WasmModuleCompilation() = default;
+
+void WasmModuleCompilation::OnBytesReceived(const uint8_t* bytes, size_t size) {
+}
+
+void WasmModuleCompilation::Finish(
+    Isolate* isolate, const ModuleCachingCallback& caching_callback,
+    const std::function<void(std::variant<Local<WasmModuleObject>, Local<Value>>
+                                 module_or_error)>& resolution_callback) {
+  resolution_callback(Exception::Error(
+      String::NewFromUtf8Literal(isolate, "WebAssembly is disabled")));
+}
+
+void WasmModuleCompilation::Abort() {}
+
+void WasmModuleCompilation::SetHasCompiledModuleBytes() {}
+
+void WasmModuleCompilation::SetMoreFunctionsCanBeSerializedCallback(
+    std::function<void(CompiledWasmModule)>) {}
+
+void WasmModuleCompilation::SetUrl(const char* url, size_t length) {}
 #endif  // !V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
 
 namespace internal {
